  "text": "# Profiling, mc3units_cil: mc3units on the cil partition, with the same config\n# and seed-csvv, in its own folder so mc3units stays as it is.\n# Batch 0, rcp85, SSP3, high, with CCSM4, GFDL-ESM2M and MIROC5 run one after\n# another in one process, as a production montecarlo worker does, with the settings of\n# montecarlo/wheat_winter-rcp85.yml, as mcunit.\n# The projection system shuffles the units, so their order may differ\n# between runs. seed-csvv is fixed to the draw of mcunit's pvals.yml, so every unit of both\n# versions uses the same coefficients. The histclim year order is a hash of\n# each unit's folder, so it matches between runs too.\n# Outputs go to scratch. The jobs pass\n# --outputdir=/scratch/midway3/$USER/agri-profiling/mc3units_cil/outputs\n# on the command line, so each user writes to their own scratch.\nimport: \"../../configs/wheat_winter_pbarspline.yml\"\nmode: montecarlo\noutputdir: /scratch/midway3/cadavidsanchez/agri-profiling/mc3units_cil/outputs\ntimeout: 12\ndo_farmers: true\ndo_historical: true\nonly-rcp: rcp85\nonly-models: [CCSM4, GFDL-ESM2M, MIROC5]\nonly-ssp: SSP3\nonly-iam: high\nonly-batch-number: 0\npvals:\n  wheat_winter-280823:\n    seed-csvv: 207090040328577895136399886809632106736\nsocioeconomic_data_dir: /project/cil/gcp/outputs_newsocioeconomics/socioeconomics/1.0.0/\n"
 },
